  "goodToKnow": "Das Abendland is the Occident, the West (Western Europe), literally the evening land where the sun sets. The opposite is das Morgenland (the Orient). The term is old-fashioned and ideologically loaded: Oswald Spengler wrote Der Untergang des Abendlandes (1918–1922), and the anti-Islam movement Pegida, founded in Dresden in 2014, used it in its name. Neutral German says der Westen. It has no plural."
